slang: no parameter-dependent errors from a generic class body checked unset

slang checks each generic class body once with its parameters unset (the
"invalid specialization": for a class nothing specialises, and for every
generic class in a package that a wildcard-import lookup force-elaborates).
Two checks there reported errors that depend on the parameters' values, on
code that is correct in every specialisation:

    class m #(int XLEN = 32);
      reg [7:0] mem [bit [XLEN-1:0]];
      function void load(string f); $readmemh(f, mem); endfunction
    endclass

"'$readmemh' cannot be called with an associative array with non-integral
index type": the index type failed to resolve, and is the error type.

    class c #(int W = 32);
      virtual ifc #(.W(W)) v;
      function void f(virtual ifc x); v = x; endfunction
    endclass

"value of type 'virtual interface ifc#(W=32)' cannot be assigned to type
'virtual interface ifc#(W=<unset>)'".

The first now skips an index of the error type; the second reports nothing
for two virtual interface types where nothing is instantiated.

Local issue SL-5 (patches/slang/README.md). Not reported upstream yet.
Present in v11.0 and on master (2026-10-16). Applies to v11.0.

